# Git Cadence

- Create a git commit after every 3 meaningful code or configuration edits.
  Every commit body references its ticket (`Refs #N` / `Closes #N`) — `/ship`
  refuses commits that don't.
- Pushing means the ticket branch and `dev`, and only through the
  verify-gated `/ship` (`scripts/agent/ship.sh`): run `/verify` first.
  Do not push `main` directly from ticket work.
- Do not include junk, generated uploads, local artifacts, secrets, or unrelated files in these commits.
- If the working tree contains unrelated user changes, keep them separate and do not revert them.
- Before committing, review `git status` and staged diff so the commit contains only intended files.
